ces","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:03:11-07:00","id":1087396,"title":"","content":"I'm unsure if I want this book honestly. I'll Buck the trend and say in general I was unhappy with Dark Eras, it was released before all the core books we're 2e and so it was a mix of 1e, 2e, and quasi 2e and ended up a huge mechanical mess. Even the London Chapter which was the one chapter I was really happy with is now reduced to rubble because Changeling 2e has been rewritten! <br /> <br /> This is also why I won't touch mortal remains. You learn to walk before you run. <br /> <br /> So I'm very leery for risk of being burned again. <br /> <br /> On the other hand if it has 2e rules for Immortals it's likely to be the only immortals rules update and it shouldn't be in conflict with future rules as such. <br /> <br /> So I guess I need to know if the Immortal rules are 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:37:48-07:00","id":1087411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1087311-dark-eras-companion-for-sale?p=1087396#post1087396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unsure if I want this book honestly. I'll Buck the trend and say in general I was unhappy with Dark Eras, it was released before all the core books we're 2e and so it was a mix of 1e, 2e, and quasi 2e and ended up a huge mechanical mess. Even the London Chapter which was the one chapter I was really happy with is now reduced to rubble because Changeling 2e has been rewritten!<br /> <br /> This is also why I won't touch mortal remains. You learn to walk before you run.<br /> <br /> So I'm very leery for risk of being burned again.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if it has 2e rules for Immortals it's likely to be the only immortals rules update and it shouldn't be in conflict with future rules as such.<br /> <br /> So I guess I need to know if the Immortal rules are 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a shame - I really enjoyed the first book and Tales of Dark Eras. Even though some mechanical aspects like Changeling may have changed - the lore concept and environment I doubt will change such as the London chapter, and that I doubt the 2E mechanics within the Dark Eras will be changed. I wish you look in your decision, and I do get where you are coming from.<br /> <br /> With that said - I really wish that instead of having to wait for an Official 2E launch for all the templates, there was a brief like 30 - 40 page 2E pamphlet for splats that are going to take some time such as Sin-Eaters &amp; Mummies. While I know there are homebrew attempts; an official update while even if minor for like 9.99$ would be nice - I know that things change in development but I assume since Mummy &amp; Sin Eater is so far away; it would be nice to have a stable usable supplement meanwhile.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Taking a look at the book - I think the Immortal rules are for 2E for the Body Thieves &amp; Blood Bathers - with that said though the section seems to only be about 8 pages? (Pg 44 - 50). I hope this helps influence your decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","user":"Volke","date":".  Immortals 05-03-2017, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:48:40-07:00","id":1087420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1087311-dark-eras-companion-for-sale?p=1087411#post1087411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a shame - I really enjoyed the first book and Tales of Dark Eras. Even though some mechanical aspects like Changeling may have changed - the lore concept and environment I doubt will change such as the London chapter, and that I doubt the 2E mechanics within the Dark Eras will be changed. I wish you look in your decision, and I do get where you are coming from. <br /> <br /> With that said - I really wish that instead of having to wait for an Official 2E launch for all the templates, there was a brief like 30 - 40 page 2E pamphlet for splats that are going to take some time such as Sin-Eaters &amp; Mummies. While I know there are homebrew attempts; an official update while even if minor for like 9.99$ would be nice - I know that things change in development but I assume since Mummy &amp; Sin Eater is so far away; it would be nice to have a stable usable supplement meanwhile. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> What use would that pamphlet be if in the development process say Geist got heavily modified from what's in the pamphlet? <br /> <br /> As for London, we know that approaches aren't a thing anymore it was based on David Hill's version of Changeling 2e, not Rose and Meghan's 2e Changeling, so it's already toast now. <br /> <br /> And with the mechanics a mess (except for the 1e mechanics, which I have no interest in), what good is the lore? <br /> <br /> So really the only part that really interests me now for the first Dark Eras is the Neolithic Mate/Werewolf and the Skin Changers/Demon Aztecs. <br /> <br /> I think I'll pass this time, at least till the Chapter with the Immortals is published separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:52:18-07:00","id":1087423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1087311-dark-eras-companion-for-sale?p=1087420#post1087420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What use would that pamphlet be if in the development process say Geist got heavily modified from what's in the pamphlet?<br /> <br /> As for London, we know that approaches aren't a thing anymore it was based on David Hill's version of Changeling 2e, not Rose and Meghan's 2e Changeling, so it's already toast now.<br /> <br /> And with the mechanics a mess (except for the 1e mechanics, which I have no interest in), what good is the lore?<br /> <br /> So really the only part that really interests me now for the first Dark Eras is the Neolithic Mate/Werewolf and the Skin Changers/Demon Aztecs.<br /> <br /> I think I'll pass this time, at least till the Chapter with the Immortals is published separately.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just think it would assist storytellers in the meanwhile (Crossover 2E require decent homebrew for the splats <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - I don't see either Geist or Mummy getting published in completion for quite sometime <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I understand your POV, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:58:05-07:00","id":1087428,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I just not willing to pay for none functional mechanics. I don't think that makes me a dick, I understand people wanted Dark Eras ASAP, but it was premature IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","